Backport of upstream DXMT 66277b82e "fix(d3d11): make pure virtual call non-fatal"
(Feifan He, MIT, 2026-09-16) to the pinned DXMT revision.

Skyrim Special Edition releases a destroyed texture a second time, and the call lands on a pure
virtual slot of a destroyed D3D11 object. The pinned revision answers that with __builtin_trap(), so
the game dies about 12 seconds after launch with "err: Pure virtual function called". Windows and
DXVK let the same stray call return harmlessly. This logs the message as before and then returns,
except in debug builds (the release build defines NDEBUG: meson `b_ndebug=if-release`).
Upstream issue: https://github.com/3Shain/dxmt/issues/231

diff --git a/src/d3d11/d3d11.cpp b/src/d3d11/d3d11.cpp
index 0550862..790b2d1 100644
--- a/src/d3d11/d3d11.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d11/d3d11.cpp
@@ -212,5 +212,7 @@ extern "C" void _massert(const char *_Message, const char *_File,
 
 extern "C" void __cxa_pure_virtual() {
   dxmt::Logger::err(dxmt::str::format("Pure virtual function called"));
+#ifndef NDEBUG
   __builtin_trap();
+#endif
 }
\ No newline at end of file
